      "name": "Landing: Offer",
      "settings": {
        "banner_text": "28 missions.\nA script for each.\nHe just shows up.",
        "heading": "The gift he’ll actually use.",
        "body": "<p>He doesn’t have to be creative. Every mission is a briefing: what he needs, how it goes, what to say. That’s why the <strong>kit </strong><em><strong>I Am Best Dad In The World</strong></em> exists.</p><p>This isn’t a parenting book. Nobody’s correcting anybody.</p><p>It’s a <strong>playbook.</strong></p><p>28 ready-made missions with clear instructions. <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">He opens the book, picks a mission and goes.</span> No Googling, no sixteen open tabs.</p>",
        "closing": "<p><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">They’ll forget the toys. They’ll remember the nonsense he did with them.</span></p>",
        "banner_bg_color": "#ee614c",
        "banner_text_color": "#ffffff",
        "banner_border_color": "#ffffff",
        "banner_shadow_color": "#2b2d45",
        "background_color": "#f6e3dc",
        "text_color": "#2b2d45",
        "marker_color": "#fbe3a8",
        "marker_opacity": 100,
        "divider_top_color": "",
        "divider_bottom_color": "#f2eee7",
        "divider_style": "waves-1-patterned_1200x20",
        "divider_animate": true
      }
    },
    "landing_excerpts_tgTUtE": {
      "type": "landing-excerpts",
      "blocks": {
        "excerpt_drVwBD": {
          "type": "excerpt",
          "settings": {
            "title": "The Indoor Camping",
            "text": "<p>Because Bugs Suck and You Love Your Couch</p><p><em>Perfect for when you need a last-minute distraction and still look like a hero. Just yell, “Surprise! We’re camping tonight!” and watch your kids lose their minds.</em></p><p><em><strong>The crap you'll need:</strong></em><em> a sheet (or a tent), pillows, blankets, flashlights, snacks.</em></p><p><em><strong>Why it works:</strong></em><em> Instant nostalgia. Your kids will remember this way longer than that time you took them to the actual wilderness and they whined the whole time.</em></p><p><em>Bottom line: Set up a tent in your house, call it camping, and enjoy all the glory of a dad who just nailed it—without even leaving the driveway. You’re welcome.</em></p>"
          }
        },
        "excerpt_Xjk7nV": {
          "type": "excerpt",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Reading",
            "text": "<p>Eventually, your kid will develop favorites. And by favorites, I mean the same book. Every. Single. Night. Welcome to the world of Reading the Same Exact Book for the 157th Time in a Row, where you could narrate it in your sleep. Actually, you probably are. Still—super important bonding moment!!!</p>"
          }
        },
        "excerpt_3JgAHr": {
          "type": "excerpt",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Pirate Treasure Hunt",
            "text": "<p>The treasure: Three soggy cookies? Sure, why not. The treasure isn’t the point. It’s the fact that it was left by freaking pirates!</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "excerpt_drVwBD",
        "excerpt_Xjk7nV",
        "excerpt_3JgAHr"
      ],
